# A real config.php holds database credentials — it belongs outside public_html
# and must never be committed. config.example.php is the committed template.
#
# The leading slash anchors this to api/config.php only. Without it the rule also
# matched api/lib/Config.php (the class), because git is case-insensitive on
# Windows and macOS — which would have deployed an API missing its config loader.
/config.php
